    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (the project's single `AcceptanceTest`, which includes the new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` checkpoint) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft (possible) duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) with getters/setters, plus their `@Column` mappings.\n\n2. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate BOOLEAN` and `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` columns. Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them.\n\n4. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 scans existing owners for one with the same normalized `lastName` and `postcode` but a different E.164 telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` true and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the matching owner id (earliest by id if several), otherwise `possibleDuplicate` false. It runs within the create transaction, after `RejectDuplicateIdentity` (hard duplicates already rejected) and before `SaveOwner` (so it can't match itself).\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignPossibleDuplicate` into the pipeline between `rejectDuplicateIdentity` and `assignHouseholdSize`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the DTO mapping picks up the two fields by name automatically; added `@Mapping(ignore = true)` for them on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (they're server-computed, not client input), consistent with the other assigned fields.\n\nThe check reads back correctly through `GET /api/owners/{id}` because the flags are persisted on the entity (like `namesakeCount`/`householdSize`) and mapped straight into the DTO.",
